-- Sync the discovery-pipeline backlog into the real /admin/review queue
-- (2026-09-29, direct user request — see this session's own conversation for
-- the full story: "push the backed up data from the venue and district
-- discovery routines through to the admin dash for my review" was first
-- (mistakenly) read as Curia Command, a separate claude.ai Artifact — the
-- user meant this app's own /admin/review, backed by venue_candidates/
-- district_candidates (migration 0010), which has sat empty since the real
-- Curator worker has never run live (CURATOR_ENABLED=false all session).
--
-- "63 venue + 4 district candidates below are the real backlog
-- from docs/data/venue-suggestions.json/district-suggestions.json's own
-- "pending" entries — genuine daily research output, but the
-- curia-suggestion-review agent that independently re-verifies each one
-- before promoting/rejecting it has stalled since 2026-09-17/18, so none of
-- this has had that pass. Loaded as status='pending_review' (the same status
-- the real Curator worker pipeline would leave a candidate at) so it shows
-- up in the real review queue, but gate1_reasoning is deliberately an honest
-- placeholder rather than a real assessment, and distinctiveness_proposed/
-- ownership are left null (the review screen shows "ownership unknown" and
-- defaults distinctiveness to 4 for editing, not a claimed real score) —
-- this migration does not pretend a review pass happened that didn't.

insert into venue_candidates (
